   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# YouTube AI-Music Monthly Counts Tutorial\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook shows how to collect a heuristic monthly time series of AI-music-related YouTube uploads using the YouTube Data API.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will:\n",
    "- Use keyword queries (e.g., \"AI generated music\", \"Suno AI\") to find videos per month\n",
    "- Page through results with a safe cap to avoid quota blow-ups\n",
    "- Fetch video details and filter to the **Music** category (categoryId = 10, verified via API)\n",
    "- Save counts to CSV and visualize the time series\n",
    "\n",
    "Notes and caveats:\n",
    "- This is a heuristic, not an official platform metric. Results depend on queries chosen and API availability.\n",
    "- We cap pagination to limit quotas; you can adjust as needed.\n",
    "- You need a YouTube Data API key for this notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "Outputs:\n",
    "- `data/youtube_ai_music_monthly.csv` with columns:\n",
    "  - `month` (YYYY-MM-01)\n",
    "  - `youtube_ai_music_count` (sum of all queries per month)\n",
    "  - `youtube_ai_music_music_category_count` (subset filtered to Music category)\n",
    "- Figures saved under `figures/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required libraries\n",
    "%pip install -q requests pandas matplotlib\n",
    "\n",
    "# If %pip is unsupported in your environment, run these in a terminal instead:\n",
    "#   pip install requests pandas matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Set your YouTube API key\n",
    "\n",
    "You can set `YOUTUBE_API_KEY` in your environment before starting the notebook (preferred), or paste it below.\n",
    "\n",
    "To set in a terminal (macOS/Linux):\n",
    "```\n",
    "export YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_key_here\n",
    "```\n",
    "On Windows (PowerShell):\n",
    "```\n",
    "$Env:YOUTUBE_API_KEY = \"your_key_here\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import datetime\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Data/figures folders\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path(\"data\")\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR = Path(\"figures\")\n",
    "DATA_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "FIGURES_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "API_KEY = os.getenv(\"YOUTUBE_API_KEY\", \"\")\n",
    "if not API_KEY:\n",
    "    # Prompt user input if env var not set\n",
    "    API_KEY = input(\"Enter your YOUTUBE_API_KEY: \").strip()\n",
    "    if not API_KEY:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\"YouTube API key is required. Set YOUTUBE_API_KEY or paste it when prompted.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "API_KEY[:8] + \"...\"  # show partial key for sanity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Utility functions and configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll define:\n",
    "- A month generator for `[start, end]`\n",
    "- Search and pagination helpers\n",
    "- Video category mapping and details lookup\n",
    "- A collector that builds monthly counts for both \"all results\" and \"Music category only\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def month_range(start_date: datetime.date, end_date: datetime.date):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generate month-start dates from start to end inclusive.\"\"\"\n",
    "    months = []\n",
    "    cur = datetime.date(start_date.year, start_date.month, 1)\n",
    "    last = datetime.date(end_date.year, end_date.month, 1)\n",
    "    while cur <= last:\n",
    "        months.append(cur)\n",
    "        if cur.month == 12:\n",
    "            cur = datetime.date(cur.year + 1, 1, 1)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            cur = datetime.date(cur.year, cur.month + 1, 1)\n",
    "    return months\n",
    "\n",
    "QUERIES = [\n",
    "    \"AI generated music\",\n",
    "    \"AI music\",\n",
    "    \"Suno AI\",\n",
    "    \"Udio AI\",\n",
    "    \"Boomy AI music\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "START = datetime.date(2023, 1, 1)\n",
    "END = datetime.date.today().replace(day=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cap pagination to avoid quota blow-ups (each page returns up to 50 videos)\n",
    "MAX_PAGES = 5  # 5 pages * 50 = up to 250 videos per query per month\n",
    "\n",
    "SEARCH_URL = \"https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/search\"\n",
    "VIDEOS_URL = \"https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/videos\"\n",
    "CATEGORIES_URL = \"https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/videoCategories\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Search and details helpers\n",
    "\n",
    "We will:\n",
    "- Search per query and month, collecting video IDs with pagination\n",
    "- Fetch the category mapping (Music is id 10) for a given region (US)\n",
    "- Fetch video details for collected IDs and filter to Music category"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def youtube_search(api_key: str, query: str, published_after: str, published_before: str, max_pages: int = MAX_PAGES):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return a list of video IDs from YouTube Search with capped pagination.\"\"\"\n",
    "    params = {\n",
    "        \"key\": api_key,\n",
    "        \"q\": query,\n",
    "        \"part\": \"snippet\",\n",
    "        \"type\": \"video\",\n",
    "        \"order\": \"date\",\n",
    "        \"maxResults\": 50,\n",
    "        \"publishedAfter\": published_after,\n",
    "        \"publishedBefore\": published_before,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    ids = []\n",
    "    next_page_token = None\n",
    "    pages = 0\n",
    "    while True:\n",
    "        if next_page_token:\n",
    "            params[\"pageToken\"] = next_page_token\n",
    "        resp = requests.get(SEARCH_URL, params=params, timeout=30)\n",
    "        if resp.status_code != 200:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        data = resp.json()\n",
    "        for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n",
    "            vid = item.get(\"id\", {}).get(\"videoId\")\n",
    "            if vid:\n",
    "                ids.append(vid)\n",
    "        next_page_token = data.get(\"nextPageToken\")\n",
    "        pages += 1\n",
    "        if not next_page_token or pages >= max_pages:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    return ids\n",
    "\n",
    "def youtube_video_categories(api_key: str, region_code: str = \"US\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fetch a mapping of categoryId -> title for a region (e.g., US).\"\"\"\n",
    "    params = {\n",
    "        \"key\": api_key,\n",
    "        \"part\": \"snippet\",\n",
    "        \"regionCode\": region_code,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    resp = requests.get(CATEGORIES_URL, params=params, timeout=30)\n",
    "    resp.raise_for_status()\n",
    "    data = resp.json()\n",
    "    mapping = {}\n",
    "    for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n",
    "        cid = item.get(\"id\")\n",
    "        title = item.get(\"snippet\", {}).get(\"title\")\n",
    "        if cid and title:\n",
    "            mapping[str(cid)] = title\n",
    "    return mapping\n",
    "\n",
    "def youtube_videos_details(api_key: str, video_ids: list):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fetch video details (including categoryId) for a list of IDs.\"\"\"\n",
    "    # API supports up to 50 IDs per call; chunk if needed.\n",
    "    details = []\n",
    "    CHUNK = 50\n",
    "    for i in range(0, len(video_ids), CHUNK):\n",
    "        chunk = video_ids[i:i+CHUNK]\n",
    "        params = {\n",
    "            \"key\": api_key,\n",
    "            \"part\": \"snippet\",\n",
    "            \"id\": \",\".join(chunk)\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        resp = requests.get(VIDEOS_URL, params=params, timeout=30)\n",
    "        if resp.status_code != 200:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        data = resp.json()\n",
    "        for item in data.get(\"items\", []):\n",
    "            vid = item.get(\"id\")\n",
    "            cat = item.get(\"snippet\", {}).get(\"categoryId\")\n",
    "            details.append({\"videoId\": vid, \"categoryId\": cat})\n",
    "    return details"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Collect monthly counts (total and Music category)\n",
    "\n",
    "We loop over months and queries, collect unique video IDs, and then count how many are under the Music category."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def collect_monthly_counts(api_key: str, start: datetime.date, end: datetime.date, queries: list, max_pages: int = MAX_PAGES):\n",
    "    months = month_range(start, end)\n",
    "    # Fetch category mapping once (US region)\n",
    "    cat_map = youtube_video_categories(api_key, region_code=\"US\")\n",
    "    # Music category is commonly id \"10\"\n",
    "    music_cat_id = None\n\",\n    "    for cid, title in cat_map.items():\n",
    "        if title.lower() == \"music\":\n",
    "            music_cat_id = cid\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    print(\"Music category id:\", music_cat_id)\n",
    "\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for m in months:\n",
    "        # Define month window [m, next_m)\n",
    "        if m.month == 12:\n",
    "            next_m = datetime.date(m.year + 1, 1, 1)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            next_m = datetime.date(m.year, m.month + 1, 1)\n",
    "        published_after = m.isoformat() + \"T00:00:00Z\"\n",
    "        published_before = next_m.isoformat() + \"T00:00:00Z\"\n",
    "\n",
    "        # Collect video IDs across queries and de-duplicate\n",
    "        all_ids = []\n",
    "        for q in queries:\n",
    "            ids = youtube_search(api_key, q, published_after, published_before, max_pages=max_pages)\n",
    "            all_ids.extend(ids)\n",
    "        unique_ids = list(set(all_ids))\n",
    "\n",
    "        total_count = len(unique_ids)\n",
    "        music_count = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "        # If we have IDs and a valid music category, fetch details to filter\n",
    "        if unique_ids and music_cat_id:\n",
    "            details = youtube_videos_details(api_key, unique_ids)\n",
    "            music_count = sum(1 for d in details if str(d.get(\"categoryId\")) == str(music_cat_id))\n",
    "\n",
    "        rows.append({\n",
    "            \"month\": m.isoformat(),\n",
    "            \"youtube_ai_music_count\": total_count,\n",
    "            \"youtube_ai_music_music_category_count\": music_count,\n",
    "        })\n",
    "        print(f\"{m.isoformat()} -> total={total_count}, music_only={music_count}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    out_path = DATA_DIR / \"youtube_ai_music_monthly.csv\"\n",
    "    df.to_csv(out_path, index=False)\n",
    "    print(\"Saved:\", out_path)\n",
    "    return df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Run the collection\n",
    "\n",
    "This may take a few minutes depending on your pagination cap and network speed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_yt = collect_monthly_counts(API_KEY, START, END, QUERIES, max_pages=MAX_PAGES)\n",
    "df_yt.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualize\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll plot the total heuristic count (sum of queries) and the music-only count on the same figure.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: The main visualization script expects `youtube_ai_music_monthly.csv` to contain at least the `youtube_ai_music_count` column; the extra `youtube_ai_music_music_category_count` column is for your analysis here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_yt = pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR / \"youtube_ai_music_monthly.csv\")\n",
    "df_yt[\"month\"] = pd.to_datetime(df_yt[\"month\"])  # ensure datetime for x-axis\n",
    "df_yt = df_yt.sort_values(\"month\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(df_yt[\"month\"], df_yt[\"youtube_ai_music_count\"], label=\"All results (sum of queries)\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "if \"youtube_ai_music_music_category_count\" in df_yt.columns:\n",
    "    plt.plot(df_yt[\"month\"], df_yt[\"youtube_ai_music_music_category_count\"], label=\"Music category only\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "plt.title(\"YouTube AI-Music Related Uploads per Month (Heuristic)\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Month\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Video count\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / \"youtube_ai_music_usage_combined.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save single-series chart for compatibility with the scripts\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(df_yt[\"month\"], df_yt[\"youtube_ai_music_count\"], marker=\"o\", linewidth=2, color=\"#1f77b4\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"YouTube AI-Music Related Uploads (Heuristic) per Month\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Month\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Video count (sum of queries)\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / \"youtube_ai_music_usage.png\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ]
